The linked GitHub repository provides a proof-of-concept for remote code execution in Redis versions 6.2.22, 7.4.9, 8.6.4, and 8.8.0.

Great read. Why are we not actually training on all possible binaries?

@random_walker: "To understand and empathize with how workers in many or most fields outside software experience advances in AI capabilities, I propose a little thought experiment. Imagine an alternate universe in which — for whatever reason — no one ever published source code online."

This thought experiment helps explain some of the issues with AI and labor by imagining a world where source code is never shared publicly.

Excited to co-found Discovery Loop with my long-time collaborators @JeffDean, @Sanjay_Ghemawat, and @OriolVinyalsML. Our mission is to automate machine learning, engineering, and science to accelerate discoveries and progress.

@JeffDean: "Announcing Discovery Loop! We are founding Discovery Loop (@DiscoLoopAI), a Public Benefit Corporation dedicated to automating machine learning, science, and engineering. The four of us have worked together for 14 to 30 years, helping build some of the most used products, infrastructure, and AI models, and we’re excited to pursue this ambitious goal."

Discovery Loop is building AI systems that automate the experimental loops of science and engineering, focusing on continuous exploration.
